      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00217:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "Benzaldehyde and cyanide form a tetrahedral intermediate, which in presence of hydrogen cyanide gives mandelonitrile (88 percent) where benzene is single-bonded to C single-bonded to hydrogen, nitrile, and hydroxyl groups."
        },
