      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00217:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "Hydrogen cyanide converts benzaldehyde to mandelonitrile. Mandelonitrile is reduced to 2-amino-1-phenylethanol using lithium aluminum hydride in tetrahydrofuran, then hydronium. It’s hydrolyzed to mandelic acid (90 percent) in hydronium with heat."
        },
